    "turn_text": "Yeah, Gabe, it does seem to be a bit of a change in tone, right? They definitely don't want to lose this message of the threat they think that Donald Trump presents, but they're trying to find a way to tie it into what she would do as president. The enemy's list coupled with the to-do list, if you will. Is this a desire to create a contrast on character, but also making sure that the policy message doesn't get lost, especially considering how short this campaign has been for the vice president?",
