    "turn_idx": 39,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, well, listen, we all remember what happened on January 6 when Donald Trump inspired a violent mob to try to overturn the results of a free and fair election. I think everybody remembers the harm that was caused that day. Of course, we will be thinking about that, but we're also going to talk about the harm that Donald Trump caused every single day when he sat behind the resolute desk. And what the Vice President is going to tell to the American people is that it doesn't have to be this way. We do not have to have leadership that traffics in chaos, that traffics in division, that celebrates violence every single day. We can actually have leadership that is focused on the people, that is focused on turning down the temperature, bringing people together and getting things done. That's what so many, particularly these undecided voters who are exhausted with the current brand of politics in the Trump era, they are looking for a new way forward. And that's exactly what the vice president has been talking about every day on the stump. And that's",
