    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80806.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think she has been talking about her policy proposals and what she wants to do in office. She's been doing that since she launched this campaign. We've put out a range of proposals to lower costs with the American people, to spur a small business growth, to make sure that American manufacturing remains right here in America. What I have not seen is Donald Trump do anything to that effect. His only economic policy that he's talked about since he's launched this campaign is another tax cut for the ultra rich. The only thing he's talking about for the middle class is across the board tax increase. He is across the board tariffs raising costs on American families by $4,000 a month. So you'll hear the Vice President talk more about her economic plans tonight where she wants to take this country. We do think it stands in stark contrast to what Donald Trump is offering up to middle class families across this country. We think it's resonating. with undecided voters who are still making up their minds over the course of this last week. We're going to make sure that they hear that.",
