  {
    "episode_id": 80806,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80806.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 65,
    "turn_text": "Well, that's what we want for everyone, right? We want to hear that our priorities, our values in Southwest Washington are reflected in the national agenda. We want to hear that reflected in DC and not DC insert itself into our lives here in an incredibly toxic way that we've seen here recently. It's really important that we're talking to people about the issues they're facing. We are hearing them when they say the prices are out of control. They're worried that they're never going to be able to own a home. They're working free jobs and they're not making rent. Those are the things that I hear all the time. I was just talking to one of the directors, one of our largest labor and delivery wards. She told me that right now, about 40% of the babies born in her hospital have at least one parent addicted to fentanyl. That is astonishing. And it feels like if this is something that was happening to what their families would have been action. We want to hear it taken seriously. And it's worth, I've put my shoulder behind in these past 20 months as a member of Congress.",
