    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/0/80806.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 69,
    "turn_text": "Well, I don't think people in my community are going to change their vote based on what I say about the presidential level. So I'm very clear personally about my value and who I'm not voting for. But we're running in a race that is feeling increasingly polarized and overshadowed by a national gender that's not talking about the experiences of living in rural America right now. So, you know, at a time when my, listen, my opponent has called for the defunding of the ATF and the FBI, he has called voting by mail sketchy. And it's really even more important that we are talking about the issues that matter to people that we are supporting the systems that undergird our values. I think that 90% of Americans agree about 90% of the issues. And so to see ourselves sort of torn apart, and, and weaponized against each other is, is really concerning.",
