    "turn_idx": 73,
    "turn_text": "Welcome back. Ohio may no longer be a presidential battleground, but it is at the heart of the fight for control of the Senate. Democratic Senator Sherrod Brown is facing Republican challenger Bernie Moreno. Brown won reelection in the state in 2018, which was sandwiched around Trump winning the state in 2016 and 2020. That means that Senator Brown is likely going to need more than a few ticket splitters to hold on to his seat. For more, Ali Vitale joins me now from Strong'sville, Ohio. So tell me, Ali, you and I have been going all across the country looking for these ticket splitters. Who are the ticket splitters in Ohio that Brown is counting on to win?",
